<title>SINGAPORE: Sri Lanka 1997 tea exports seen at 250 million kg.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka 1997 tea exports seen at 250 million kg.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's tea exports will reach 250 million kg in 1997, equalling expected 1996 exports, the director-general of the Sri Lanka Tea Board said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have the same export target of 250 million kilos for next year,&quot; Ranjith Maligaspe, the tea board director-general, told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>He said tea exports this calender year would hit an all-time high of 250 million kg. Exports in 1995 were about 245 million kg.</p>
<p>Sri Lanka is the world's biggest exporter of tea.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
</text>
